{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1448274-around-the-world","id":1448274,"title":"Around the World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-11T17:58:29-07:00","id":1448274,"title":"Around the World","content":"Since I am currently stuck in the hospital I figured I'd open up the floor to discussions of a general nature- Nomes, Merets, cults, whatever. Arisen far and wide and what motivates them. Starting off with a question. We know Arisen were in America well before Columbus. How did they get there? Please throw out your most likely and most entertaining scenarios. I'll come up with a few of my own. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T19:26:00-07:00","id":1448284,"title":"","content":"Maybe they hitched a ride on the Norse vessels who sailed to America? A Norse warrior-cult who reveres the sleeping body of a &quot;true einherjar&quot; who will awaken in the face of a glorious battle in the mortal realms, and to raid infidels for masterwork relics to arm his brothers-in-arms in Valhalla, sounds good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T02:24:16-07:00","id":1448304,"title":"","content":"There's also the possibility of the Tier 3 level of Palace Knows its Pharaoh:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mummies with Sekhem 8 or higher may open a door to an unknown destination within the greater contiguous structure, leaving the egress point to Fate to determine. Rarely, this leads to another doorway on another continent entirely, making the unleashing Epic. This Utterance is how mummies traversed the world and ensconced themselves in mortal cultures after the First Sothic Turn. </div> </div> </div>Besides that, they could have been thrown there by the Rite of Return itself as it crumpled spacetime, placed there before Irem's fall, having gotten over there by good old fashioned sailing of their own, making use of a Vessel like the 1e Book of Sailing the Sea of Stars...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T04:45:04-07:00","id":1448307,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile I\u2019m trying to figure out the context in which the Deathless could\u2019ve arrived in Korea (other than \u2018cosmic\u2019 stuff like ajf115 said above). Sure, <i>getting</i> here is easy enough... but what \u2018dressing\u2019 should/could I give them? (And <i>I\u2019m</i> the native here, for crying out loud!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T08:33:40-07:00","id":1448423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1448274-around-the-world?p=1448307#post1448307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile I\u2019m trying to figure out the context in which the Deathless could\u2019ve arrived in Korea (other than \u2018cosmic\u2019 stuff like ajf115 said above). Sure, <i>getting</i> here is easy enough... but what \u2018dressing\u2019 should/could I give them? (And <i>I\u2019m</i> the native here, for crying out loud!)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That depends on when you want them to arrive and why they went there. I'd start with whatever drew them to the area- powerful source of Sekhem? Dangerous cult of sorcerers? Inspired by the echoes of imperialism or statism or whatever that reminds them of the nameless empire? Specific ambitions of one of the Guilds? Those are the big factors I can think of. Time period is important. Arisen arriving last year are different from Arisen arriving in 700 BC, obviously. How much a role you want them to play in the background of your city or the country is a big factor here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T12:50:10-07:00","id":1448455,"title":"","content":"Possible entries for Mummies:<br /> <br /> 1. Bering Strait. The original passage from the old world to the new world! There are some indications of cultural exchange between native peoples of Alaska and Chukotka sides of the Strait, implying that there have in fact been an unknown number of crossings by various tribes well before Columbus. Attached an arisen cult to your favorite ancient steppe nomadic empire, give them a reason to be curious of what's beyond, and there you go.<br /> <br /> 2. Polynesians are speculated to have visited America sometime between 700 AD and 1200 AD based on various records of fauna and flora the Americas have in common with Oceania. Polynesians are some of the greatest navigators in human history, having guided what are essentially floating logs vast distances across the Pacific by start patterns alone. An Arisen based on one of the Pacific islands or South Asian nations could have a cult attached to a Polynesian group or at the least be in contact with some of the islanders and hear of these great landmasses across the sea.<br /> <br /> 3. The first Emperor of China called for two separate voyages in search of a mythical island where supposedly the secret of eternal life was kept by a group of immortals. Some people think Japan was discovered by these voyagers. But it could have been the Americas instead. And he was not the only Emperor interested in the location of said island or immortality. You could justify any number of expeditions staged in China or nations in their sphere of influence with similar legends, and any mention of immortals is gonna attract Arisen attention. <br /> <br /> 4. We have several candidates for ancient sea farers. Phoenicians and by extension Carthaginians were famous for such, performing such feats as circumnavigating Africa at the request of Pharaoh and of course establishing a far flung trade empire. Carthage is in fact used as the vehicle to get the first Meret to Brazil in the Rio setting book. The Greeks were also avid colonizers and explorers, although they didn't get as far as Carthage (but with a little push from the Arisen and a helpful Utterance or two to bring them good fortune at sea...). The Minoans are a more ancient sea farer that could still be justified. Then too, the Bronze Age collapse was instigated in part by numerous tribes we just call the Sea Peoples...and we aren't entirely sure what happened to them, where they came from or where they went....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T05:39:21-07:00","id":1448498,"title":"","content":"Because this joke is hilarious to me, Jaredite dishboats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T06:51:10-07:00","id":1448501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1448274-around-the-world?p=1448423#post1448423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That depends on when you want them to arrive and why they went there. I'd start with whatever drew them to the area- powerful source of Sekhem? Dangerous cult of sorcerers? Inspired by the echoes of imperialism or statism or whatever that reminds them of the nameless empire? Specific ambitions of one of the Guilds? Those are the big factors I can think of. Time period is important. Arisen arriving last year are different from Arisen arriving in 700 BC, obviously. How much a role you want them to play in the background of your city or the country is a big factor here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! And maybe a powerful relic with an important backstory. That's another good reason for at least one mummy to show up. Could be more than one if he brought a meret or if one or more rival mummy's want the honor of un-relicing (its a word now, shut up) the vessel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T06:58:45-07:00","id":1448502,"title":"","content":"One answer that hasn't been brought up, despite being a major feature of the Dreams of Avarice <i>chronicle </i>(as opposed to the book), is the Plain of Bones, a bit of Iremite mysticism/cosmological strata/little-i infrastructure that has outposts in various places and allows the walker to go anywhere in the world.<br /> <br /> Also, obligatory but not over going on it, the exploitation of various other powers that act in the world goes a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T19:20:22-07:00","id":1448560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1448274-around-the-world?p=1448498#post1448498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because this joke is hilarious to me, Jaredite dishboats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funny you should say that. If I ever ran a game set in Salt Lake City I'd straight up find a way to shoe horn this bit into the setting. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Smith_Papyri#:~:text=The%20Joseph%20Smith%20Papyri%20(JSP,the%20Latter%20Day%20Saint%20movement\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph...int%20movement</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T17:41:24-07:00","id":1448643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1448274-around-the-world?p=1448560#post1448560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Funny you should say that. If I ever ran a game set in Salt Lake City I'd straight up find a way to shoe horn this bit into the setting. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Smith_Papyri#:~:text=The%20Joseph%20Smith%20Papyri%20(JSP,the%20Latter%20Day%20Saint%20movement\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph...int%20movement</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Christ, that'd be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:25:06-07:00","id":1449003,"title":"","content":"I've been reading Dark Eras 1, and it mentions Arisen using a piece of G-M infrastructure in Great Zimbabwe to appear in Teotihuacan.<br /> <br /> That said, they'd only be appearing 70 years before Cortez arrived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T20:30:04-07:00","id":1449310,"title":"","content":"I think it doesn\u2019t usually come up because while you can can travel to many places in the world through the plain of bones, the problem is that it\u2019s implied that gate is one of the last, if not the last method of reliable ingress to the plain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}